      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "cYuwa",
          "name": "Notes Title",
          "fill": "$accent",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Implementation notes (not part of the section)",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": 16,
          "fontWeight": "600"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "th4eA",
          "name": "Note 1",
          "fill": "#FFFFFF",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Placement: below the positioning section, above the quote and attribution block. One H2 for the section; the section label above it follows the existing section-label pattern.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "rZRwu",
          "name": "Note 2",
          "fill": "#FFFFFF",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Semantics: figure containing the brief, a list of four department rows, and a figcaption with the two disclosure lines. The H2 names the figure. The link under the figure is a plain anchor to the department cards (needs an id on that section). No button or CTA in the section.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "TB9Rw",
          "name": "Note 3",
          "fill": "#FFFFFF",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Status is text in every row: Done, Stopped, Waiting on you. The chip fill and border only reinforce it: Stopped is a solid light chip, Waiting on you is gold outlined, Done is grey outlined.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "W5fIDW",
          "name": "Note 4",
          "fill": "#FFFFFF",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Contrast on the dark ground: white on #141414 about 18:1; secondary #848484 on #0E0E0E about 5.2:1 and on #141414 about 4.9:1; gold #C9A962 on #141414 about 8:1. Do not use tertiary #737373 for captions here (below 4.5:1).",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "y2xW3a",
          "name": "Note 5",
          "fill": "#FFFFFF",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Responsive: desktop 1440 uses a brief card, a connector and three-column rows. At 390 the rows stack, each with name and chip on one line and the status line wrapping below. At 320 the chip drops under the department name and the Engineering line (the longest) wraps to four lines with no horizontal overflow.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "m7ul13",
          "name": "Note 6",
          "fill": "#FFFFFF",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Tokens: radius 0, #0A0A0A page, #0E0E0E figure, #141414 cards, #2A2A2A borders, gold #C9A962, Cormorant Garamond for the H2, Inter for the rest. No numbers, durations or counts in the section.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
